        "original_id": "1295317e-cb01-5481-a1b6-2a9f3917928c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mervyn Peake, Robert Erskine Childers\n- Products: Gormenghast books, The Riddle of the Sands, Asgard, Titus Alone\n- Topics: British literature, Fenian revolutionary activity\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Erskine Childers was born on 25 June 1870 and died on 24 November 1922.\n- Robert Erskine Childers was universally known as Erskine Childers.\n- Robert Erskine Childers was a British writer whose works included the influential novel The Riddle of the Sands.\n- Robert Erskine Childers was a Fenian revolutionary who smuggled guns to Ireland in his sailing yacht Asgard.\n- Titus Alone is a novel by Mervyn Peake that was first published in 1959.\n- Mervyn Peake is best known for the works usually referred to as the Gormenghast books.",
